  samples. 0.5 to 1.0 alone gave +0.001829 (+11.5 sigma) on full validation, which
  transferred to public as +0.0017 against +0.0018 predicted. Two points cannot distinguish
  a curve still climbing from one that has already turned over, and the practical
  consequences differ completely: still climbing means push past 2.0; turned over
  means 1.0 was the optimum and the remaining headroom is elsewhere. Prediction: NOT
  yet turned over, because the teacher is itself only 0.690168 local while the student
  sits at 0.686510, so teacher signal remains to absorb. Counter-consideration, recorded
  so the result reads either way: dozken reports his best distilled model peaking
  at epoch 3 and DECLINING after, so over-regularising toward the teacher is a real
  failure mode, not hypothetical. If 2.0 lands below v028 by more than 0.000317 the
  optimum is at or below 1.0 and this axis is closed.'
change_vs_parent: loss.distill_weight 1.0 -> 2.0 only. gamma stays absent (0), so
  the teacher term is weighted exactly as in v028; this isolates the weight and nothing
  else.
